      {
        "body": "Second-candle adverse movement is own-open minus low for a bullish reversal, high minus own-open for bearish. The geometry denominator includes only eventual same-direction second candles; the eligible-next-bar count and success rate expose selection. Complete leg duration includes the reversal and all same-colour successors through the last one, excluding right-censored legs. Its clock difference is a proxy; zero is observed tied timestamps and missing remains null. Saved 95% intervals use export-date cluster draws. Native units are product ticks for movement and minutes for duration; GC 6 is included as labelled and does not substitute for missing GC 20.",
        "id": "methods",
        "kind": "text",
        "title": "Definitions and methods"
      },
      {
        "body": "Historical import was not newly revalidated; original short-export inputs are missing. Bar open/close timing, timezone, session boundaries and provisional chart identity remain unverified. Conditioning on the future candle close is not an observable real-time entry rule. Window rankings and same-sample selections are excluded here; no stop ordering, fills, costs or profitability are established.",
        "id": "limitations",
        "kind": "text",
        "title": "Limitations and uncertainty"
      },
